  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Mission Systems obligated $460M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems received 38 awards in that period, with an average award size of $12.1M, and obligations were up 31.1% year over year. Engineering Services is the dominant market for General Dynamics Mission Systems, accounting for $418M of obligations in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems also recorded obligations in specialized manufacturing and services categories, including Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $15.6M, Security Systems Services at $13.6M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $7.7M. Historical fiscal-year obligations for General Dynamics Mission Systems show a sequence of totals: FY21 $379M, FY22 $336M, FY23 $357M, FY24 $430M, FY25 $351M, and FY26 $460M. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. This snapshot highlights where federal obligations are concentrated and how current-year obligating activity compares with the last five full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are General Dynamics Mission Systems' biggest markets?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the biggest market for General Dynamics Mission Systems at $418M in FY2026 to date. Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance follows at $15.6M, and Security Systems Services follows at $13.6M. Several manufacturing and software categories appear at lower levels, including Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $7.7M and Software Publishers at $143K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has General Dynamics Mission Systems' federal business trended over time?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Mission Systems' fiscal-year obligations moved from $379M in FY21 to $336M in FY22, $357M in FY23, $430M in FY24, $351M in FY25, and $460M in FY26. General Dynamics Mission Systems recorded year-over-year growth of up 31.1% for FY2026 to date relative to the prior period. The FY2026 total is a fiscal year to date figure and partial for the year."
      }
    ]
  },
